    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0512" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7151</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Lima</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Handley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-06T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 6, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs for Peru has telegraphed Peruvian-Minister at
                    [Berlin] to demand his passport and to turn over Peruvian interests to the
                    Minister of Spain German Minister at Lima given his passport October 6, 12 noon,
                    and will probably proceed to Chile.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Handley</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
